    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "type": "multiple",
    "prompt": "An application needs both a schema-constrained final JSON response and schema-constrained arguments for its create_draft tool. The selected model supports both features. Using the direct Messages API fields documented in the cited structured-output reference, which two configurations address the two output surfaces? Select 2 answers.",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "Use only a JSON-only instruction and a JSON parser for the final response, treating successful parsing as schema enforcement.",
        "explanation": "Parsing establishes JSON syntax, not required fields, types, or other schema constraints. A prompt-only instruction is not the documented constrained-decoding configuration."
      },
      {
        "text": "Set output_config.format to the supported JSON schema for the final response.",
        "explanation": "This feature constrains the direct response structure. It is distinct from constraining the arguments of a tool call."
      },
      {
        "text": "Enable strict: true on the create_draft tool with its supported input schema.",
        "explanation": "Strict tool use constrains tool names and inputs to their schema. It does not by itself specify the structure of the final response text."
      },
      {
        "text": "Put both schemas only into output_config.format and let its final-response grammar govern tool arguments too.",
        "explanation": "The final-response grammar does not apply to tool-use blocks. Separate strict tool configuration is needed for the second surface."
      }
    ],
