    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "type": "multiple",
    "prompt": "Under Claude Messages API version 2026-10-21, an assistant response contains only client tools: lookup_parts with id call_parts and estimate_delivery with id call_delivery. The application completes lookup_parts, but estimate_delivery fails with an upstream timeout. It is continuing the conversation rather than retrying the failed tool immediately. Which continuation actions are required to represent both calls faithfully? Select 3 answers.",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "Append the assistant response content, including both original tool_use blocks, to conversation history unchanged.",
        "explanation": "The continuation must preserve the tool requests that the following results answer. Replacing that content with a paraphrase loses the tool-call context and identifiers."
      },
      {
        "text": "Immediately follow it with a user message whose tool_result blocks use call_parts and call_delivery as their respective tool_use_id values.",
        "explanation": "Results are correlated by tool_use_id, not arrival order or tool name. The user result message must directly follow the assistant tool-use message, with result blocks before any other text."
      },
      {
        "text": "Represent the delivery timeout as a successful empty delivery estimate so the model can continue without an error branch.",
        "explanation": "An upstream failure is not evidence that no delivery estimate exists. Presenting it as successful empty data hides the execution failure and can mislead downstream reasoning."
      },
      {
        "text": "Set is_error to true on the delivery result and include a useful, non-secret timeout description.",
        "explanation": "The client-tool result format explicitly supports signaling execution failure with is_error. An informative error lets the model distinguish unavailable evidence from a valid empty result."
      }
    ],
